 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "Find the distance between the points $A({=x1}, {=y1})$, $B({=x2}, {=y2})$. Give the answer in unit length.",
 "answer": "h",
 "solution": [
  "Draw the right triangle AKB with the right angle at K, where K is the point with the x-coordinate of one point and the y-coordinate of the other.",
  "$AK=|{=x2}-({=x1})|={=dx}$ and $KB=|{=y2}-({=y1})|={=dy}$.",
  "$(AB)^2=({=dx})^2+({=dy})^2={=dx*dx}+{=dy*dy}={=h*h}$",
  "AB = {=h} unit length."
 ],
